* tshrc -- tsh runs these commands when it starts (man tsh).
*
* Where to look for a command that is neither in memory nor in the
* execution directory.  When booting from the FujiNet, /H0 is the
* tether's disk.
path /DD/CMDS /H0/CMDS
*
* The prompt is OS9: as for the Shell.  To see the data directory in it:
* PROMPT="%d: "
* (%d is the data directory, %w the last name in it, %h the history
* number, %e the last exit status, %t the time.)
*
* Aliases: the first word of a command, replaced.
alias h history
